// Vitest Snapshot v1, https://vitest.dev/guide/snapshot.html

exports[`documents named-window commands offline: "agent" 1`] = `
"Usage: opencove agent stop --node <id> [options]

Stop the agent session bound to a canvas node

Stop an agent window, or a terminal that still hosts a live observed agent, while keeping the canvas node. A terminal’s entire session stops, including its shell. An exited agent is a no-op even if its shell is still running. Plain terminals are refused; use session kill --session <id> to stop a shell session. Remote targets are refused before dispatch because safe agent-only stopping is not supported there yet.

Returns {nodeId, sessionId, stopped: true} when the stop is requested. An already-exited session returns stopped: false and reason: not_running (exit 0). A changed node/session binding refuses the stop (exit 2); inspect the node again before deciding what to stop. Stopping never sends terminal input.

Options:
  --node <id>         Select a canvas node by its ID; also accepts @self, an exact name or a unique ID prefix (6+ characters) (required)
  --space <selector>  Require every node selector, including full IDs, to belong to this space; also accepts @self, an exact name or a unique ID prefix (6+ characters)
  --project <id>      Narrow target lookup to a project; also accepts @self, an exact name or a unique ID prefix (6+ characters)

Table output (-o table): not supported.
Projectable fields: nodeId, sessionId, stopped, reason

Projection example:
  opencove agent stop --node '<id>' --fields nodeId
  {"nodeId":"node-123","sessionId":"session-123","stopped":true}

Examples:
  opencove agent stop --node "Lead"

Global options: see "opencove --help".
"
`;

exports[`documents named-window commands offline: "node" 1`] = `
"Usage: opencove node update agent --node <id> [options]

Update an agent node

Rename this window and keep its name when the agent session changes. The name is saved as provided, with surrounding whitespace removed. Use --frame to also move or resize it.

Options:
  --node <id>         Select a canvas node by its ID; also accepts @self, an exact name or a unique ID prefix (6+ characters) (required)
  --title <text>      Set a fixed window name; omit on creation to keep automatic titles
  --frame <json>      Set x, y, width and height as a JSON object; appliedFrame and frameAdjusted report any changes
  --space <selector>  Require every node selector, including full IDs, to belong to this space; also accepts @self, an exact name or a unique ID prefix (6+ characters)
  --project <id>      Narrow target lookup to a project; also accepts @self, an exact name or a unique ID prefix (6+ characters)

Table output (-o table): not supported.
Projectable fields: id, kind, title, projectId, spaceId, frame, frame.x, frame.y, frame.width, frame.height, status, sessionId, data, data.kind, data.provider, data.prompt, data.model, data.effectiveModel, data.executionDirectory, data.expectedDirectory, data.taskId

Projection example:
  opencove node update agent --node '<id>' --fields id,title
  {"revision":1,"node":{"id":"n","title":"Agent"}}

Examples:
  opencove node update agent --node node-123 --title "Lead"
  opencove node update agent --node node-123 --title "Release review" --pretty

Global options: see "opencove --help".
"
`;

