exports[`documents named-window commands offline: "project" 1`] = `
"Usage: opencove project add --path <dir> [options]

Add a local directory as a project

The path must be an existing absolute local directory on the Worker. An existing project at the same path is reused with its saved name. Agents cannot add projects: ask the user to add the project in OpenCove.

Options:
  --path <dir>   Add this local directory (required)
  --name <name>  Name a new project; defaults to the directory name

Table output (-o table): not supported.
Projectable fields: id, name, path, defaultSpace, defaultSpace.id, defaultSpace.name, defaultSpace.directoryPath, defaultSpace.rect, defaultSpace.rect.x, defaultSpace.rect.y, defaultSpace.rect.width, defaultSpace.rect.height

Projection example:
  opencove project add --path '<dir>' --fields id
  {"id":"project-123"}

Examples:
  opencove project add --path /workspace/app --name "App"

Global options: see "opencove --help".
"
`;

exports[`documents named-window commands offline: "space" 1`] = `
"Usage: opencove space create --name <name> [--project <selector>] [--directory <path>] | --name <name> --in <selector> [--frame <json>] [--move <selector>]...

Create a top-level or child space

Top-level spaces use your terminal node’s current project unless --project is given; outside OpenCove, supply --project. Placement is automatic. --directory must be an existing absolute local directory within the project’s default mount; symlinks cannot escape that mount. Omit it to use the mount root.

With --in, create a child space in the selected parent and inherit its directory. --move selects direct members of that parent. Without --frame, the boundary encloses the moved nodes, or defaults to 420×300 at the parent’s center. The server fits the boundary inside the parent, preserves room for moved nodes, and grows ancestors when needed. The result reports rect as {x,y,width,height} in canvas coordinates.

Options:
  --name <name>         Name the new space (required)
  --project <selector>  Select the project, or narrow the parent lookup; also accepts @self, an exact name or a unique ID prefix (6+ characters)
  --directory <path>    Set a top-level space’s working directory
  --in <selector>       Create inside a parent space; accepts @self, an exact ID, exact name or unique ID prefix (6+ characters)
  --frame <json>        Set the child boundary: {"x":0,"y":0,"width":420,"height":300}; requires --in
  --move <selector>     Move a node from the parent; repeat for more nodes. Accepts @self, an exact ID, exact name or unique ID prefix (6+ characters); requires --in

Table output (-o table): not supported.
Projectable fields: id, name, projectId, parentSpaceId, rect, rect.x, rect.y, rect.width, rect.height, directoryPath, movedNodeIds

Projection example:
  opencove space create --name '<name>' --fields id
  {"id":"space-123"}

Examples:
  opencove space create --name "Review"
  opencove space create --name "Migration" --project project-123 --directory /workspace/migration
  opencove space create --name "Review notes" --in @self --move "Brief" --move "Checklist"

Global options: see "opencove --help".
"
`;

